# Build output. Everything under /dist is generated: `npm run build`,
# `npm run build:prod` and `scripts/build.mjs` recreate it from source, and
# `npm run clean` (rimraf ./dist) deletes it. Tracking it was the source of a
# long-standing contradiction - `/dist/server/` was ignored here while three
# files inside it (app.js, app.js.map, package.json) were tracked, and
# gitignore has no effect on already-tracked files. The tracked artefacts were
# also frozen at the Angular 4.4.6 era (inline/vendor/main/polyfills/styles
# `.bundle.js` names, a sw-precache service-worker.js, glyphicons-halflings
# fonts and assets/tech/bootstrap.svg, all of which were removed from the
# sources during the Bootstrap-to-Material migration), so a fresh clone shipped
# a stale bundle that no build could reproduce. One blanket anchored rule
# replaces the five narrow ones; nothing legitimate lives under /dist.
/out-tsc/
/dist/
